# CABLE HOOK

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Cable Hook is an explosive rotational resistance exercise designed to develop transverse-plane power, rotational sequencing and horizontal force production.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer resistance exercises for improving hook punching mechanics and rotational striking performance.

---

# Philosophy

A powerful hook is generated by rotation, not by the arm.

Force originates from the ground, accelerates through the hips and trunk, and is transmitted into the fist through an efficient kinetic chain.

The Cable Hook overloads rotational force production while preserving combat-specific movement patterns.

CAS uses the Cable Hook to improve rotational explosiveness with minimal unnecessary fatigue.

